NAME

ulibSetFileData - Change file catalogue entry information


SYNOPSIS

void ulibSetFileData(struct FileCat *f, long AccessType, long Data)
                            a0               d0             d1


DESCRIPTION

This function sets a variable in the file catalogue structure pointed to by
<f> to the value of <Data>.

The <AccessType> parameter may be any one of the #define'd XFD_ codes in
xenolink.h (such as XFD_NAME, XFD_DESCRIPTION, etc.)

The <Data> parameter is either:

   1. An integer (for integral file fields)

   2. A pointer to a string (for certain string variables such FileName,
      Uploader, Description).

   3. A pointer to a (struct TimeDate) (for XFD_DATE_UPLOADED,
      XFD_LAST_DOWNLOADED).


CAUTION!  In the case of setting the file description, Xenolink will first
free an existing file description pointed to by <f->Description> (unless
<f->Description> is NULL), before allocating space for the new description.

It is recommended that you use ulibSetFileData() and ulibFreeFileData() to
handle file descriptions, rather than using the XFD_DESCRIPTION parameter
to this function, to avoid confusing yourself.


NOTE: This function does no checking on the data you give it, so you must
      ensure that you do not pass it too long a string.

      Check the various #define's for constants used in the file structure;
      for example, USERNAME_LENGTH characters are reserved for the file
      uploader's name; since this includes the null-terminator, the maximum
      length of the uploader's name is (USERNAME_LENGTH-1) characters.

      The situation is analagous for the other string fields.


